# Gitignored files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates: `--worktree`, a subagent with
# `isolation: worktree`, and desktop parallel sessions. Only files that are also gitignored are
# copied, so nothing tracked is duplicated.
#
# This hands live Jira and GitHub credentials to every such worktree, a subagent's included. That
# is the point — rule 3 puts all agent work in a worktree, and a worktree could not run
# `solve:once` at all — but it is a widening, not a convenience.
#
# It copies rather than links, so a worktree keeps the values it was born with: change
# REPAIR_ROUND in the primary checkout and an existing worktree will not see it.
#
# Does not apply to a worktree made by hand with `git worktree add`, nor when a WorktreeCreate
# hook replaces the default git logic.
